Issue:
Error Number: 1205, Severity: 13, State: 80, Line: 1130, Message: Transaction (Process ID 137) was deadlocked on communication buffer | generic waitable object resources with another process and has been chosen as the deadlock victim. Rerun the transaction.

Solution :
OPTION (MAXDOP 1) is a query hint in Microsoft SQL Server that forces the query optimizer to use only one CPU core (i.e., no parallelism) when executing that specific query.

What it does
MAXDOP = Maximum Degree of Parallelism
Setting it to 1 means:
The query runs serially (single-threaded)
SQL Server will not split the workload across multiple CPUs
When it’s useful
Preventing excessive CPU usage from parallel queries
Avoiding parallelism overhead on small or fast queries
Troubleshooting performance issues caused by parallel execution
Reducing contention in high-concurrency systems
